    item-213 at level 2: section_header: Discussion
      item-214 at level 3: inline: group group
        item-215 at level 4: text: This paper reports for the first ... similar to what was found in Goldberg 
        item-216 at level 4: text: et al
        item-217 at level 4: text: ., which explored ecological and ... ctors associated with TAS failure [7].
      item-218 at level 3: text: Though diagnostic test used was  ...  FTS was more sensitive than ICT [45].
      item-219 at level 3: inline: group group
        item-220 at level 4: text: Elevation was the only environme ... us studies [8,31], including Goldberg 
        item-221 at level 4: text: et al
        item-222 at level 4: text: . [7], who used a cutoff of 200  ... ich impact vector chances of survival.
      item-223 at level 3: inline: group group
        item-224 at level 4: text: The small number of failures ove ... ed in the bivariate analyses, such as 
        item-225 at level 4: text: Culex
        item-226 at level 4: text:  vector, higher population densi ... cisions. Other models have shown that 
        item-227 at level 4: text: Culex
        item-228 at level 4: text:  as the predominant vector in a district, compared to 
        item-229 at level 4: text: Anopheles
        item-230 at level 4: text: , results in more intense interv ... search has shown the opposite [15,16].
      item-231 at level 3: inline: group group
        item-232 at level 4: text: All other variables included in  ... TAS failure in our analysis. Goldberg 
        item-233 at level 4: text: et al
        item-234 at level 4: text: . found 
        item-235 at level 4: text: Brugia
        item-236 at level 4: text:  spp. to be significantly associ ... to the small number of districts with 
        item-237 at level 4: text: Brugia
        item-238 at level 4: text:  spp. in our dataset (6%) compared to 46% in the Goldberg 
        item-239 at level 4: text: et al
        item-240 at level 4: text: . article [7]. MDA coverage leve ... are not necessary to lower prevalence.
      item-241 at level 3: text: Limitations to this study includ ...  reducing LF prevalence [41,48,51–53].
      item-242 at level 3: text: Fourteen districts were excluded ... ta to extreme outliners in a district.
      item-243 at level 3: text: As this analysis used data acros ... of individuals included in the survey.
      item-244 at level 3: text: This paper provides evidence fro ... th high baseline and/or low elevation.
